const cache = new ProfileCache(new Redis(process.env.REDIS_URL!), (id) => db.profiles.findById(id));

app.get("/users/:id/profile", async (req, res) => {
  const profile = await cache.get(req.params.id);
  if (!profile) return res.sendStatus(404);
  res.json(profile);
});

app.put("/users/:id/profile", async (req, res) => {
  const updated = await db.profiles.update(req.params.id, req.body);
  await cache.invalidate(req.params.id);
  res.json(updated);
});
```

Behavior:
- Cache-aside, 300 s TTL. Missing users cached 30 s.
- Redis read or write failure falls back to DB.
- Writes delete the key. A load in flight during a write can re-cache the old value, stale for at most 300 s.
- Bump `v1` in the key when the profile shape changes.

Security warning: the key is the user id only. If the response differs per viewer (private fields, owner-only data), do not use this as is. One viewer would receive another viewer's version. Cache only the public shape, or add the viewer scope to the key.

